(7599600, 1227523, 3306, '<td valign="top">Wow! My first car was a 1959 TR3.  I bought it in 11th grade in 1968. It was not in great shape when I bought it for $750. I restored it cosmetically. It ran pretty good except I did not realize that the previous owner had put a 1957 starter in it and it kept jamming. I would have to use the hand crank to get it going! I loved that car!! It became impractical and I traded it in on a Triumph GT6+. It was like a hardtop hatchback spitfire with more horsepower. I loved that car also! Anyway, thanks for taking me down memory lane. I believe this one is a 1962 in beautiful shape. probably would sell for the low 30''s. I''ve actually been looking at them online which is an interesting coincidence. Even watched a few U Tube video''s. Love the sound of the engine. You have done a great job with this image. Great perspective and really cool in B&amp;W.  You have truly touched my emotions!!!! 10 from me :)</td>', 'Wow! My first car was a 1959 TR3.  I bought it in 11th grade in 1968. It was not in great shape when I bought it for $750. I restored it cosmetically. It ran pretty good except I did not realize that the previous owner had put a 1957 starter in it and it kept jamming. I would have to use the hand crank to get it going! I loved that car!! It became impractical and I traded it in on a Triumph GT6+. It was like a hardtop hatchback spitfire with more horsepower. I loved that car also! Anyway, thanks for taking me down memory lane. I believe this one is a 1962 in beautiful shape. probably would sell for the low 30''s. I''ve actually been looking at them online which is an interesting coincidence. Even watched a few U Tube video''s. Love the sound of the engine. You have done a great job with this image. Great perspective and really cool in B&W.  You have truly touched my emotions!!!! 10 from me :)', '2018-10-28 21:42:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7599604, 1227596, 114285, '<td valign="top">Funny</td>', 'Funny', '2018-10-28 22:45:28.000000', NULL, 1),
